### Hireflow API — local manual smoke requests
#
# Local, cookie/CSRF-aware examples for the "VS Code REST Client" extension (or any
# .http-compatible tool). Contains no credentials, live IDs, or tokens — every value
# below is a synthetic placeholder for local development only.
#
# Cookie/CSRF sequence, every time you start a fresh session:
#   1. Run "1. Prime CSRF token" below. The response sets an XSRF-TOKEN cookie.
#   2. Copy that cookie's value from the response and paste it as @xsrfToken below.
#   3. Run "2. Register" (or "3. Login" if the account already exists). The response
#      sets the Hireflow.Auth session cookie your client now holds for this host.
#   4. GET requests need no further setup. Every other mutating request also needs a
#      fresh CSRF token/header pair — repeat steps 1–2 if X-XSRF-TOKEN is rejected.
#
# Adjust @host if your API isn't on the default `docker compose` port (8080); a plain
# `dotnet run` from Hireflow.Api instead listens on http://localhost:5006 by default.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@xsrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_XSRF-TOKEN_COOKIE_VALUE_FROM_STEP_1
@email = dev-{{$timestamp}}@example.com
@password = DevPassword123!

### 0. Health check (anonymous, no cookies needed)
GET {{host}}/api/health

### 1. Prime CSRF token — copy the XSRF-TOKEN cookie from this response into @xsrfToken above
GET {{host}}/api/auth/csrf

### 2. Register a new account (sets the session cookie for this client)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "displayName": "Dev Example"
}

### 3. Login (alternative to registering, once an account already exists)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 4. Who am I
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### 5. Create a workspace (repeat step 1 first if X-XSRF-TOKEN is rejected)
POST {{host}}/api/workspaces
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{
  "name": "Example Workspace"
}

### 6. List my workspaces
GET {{host}}/api/workspaces

### 7. Workspace recruiting overview — replace {workspaceId} with a real ID from step 5/6
GET {{host}}/api/workspaces/{workspaceId}/overview

### 8. Create a job opening under that workspace
POST {{host}}/api/workspaces/{workspaceId}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}

{
  "title": "Example Role",
  "description": "Optional description"
}

### 9. Log out
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrfToken}}
